%% cranelisp-frontend current-state — Sprint 87 Stage B audit.
%% Refreshes audits/frontend-20260423-current-state.mmd (superseded, kept in place
%% per the never-delete-archived rule). Delta vs predecessor: the dual REPL/batch
%% top-level entry pair (build_repl_input / build_top_level) is GONE — replaced by
%% one per-form dispatcher build_form + one sequence boundary build_forms; the
%% synthetic-span allocator is now centralized; name resolution is deferred to int.
%% Remaining structural notes mark the S87 findings (F1, F2, F4, F5, F7).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Caller as int orchestrator / REPL / Tests
    participant API as cranelisp_frontend::lib (facade re-exports)
    participant Reader as reader.rs (hand-written rec-descent)
    participant Mod as module_extract.rs
    participant QQ as quasiquote.rs
    participant DM as defmacro.rs
    participant Span as next_synthetic_span() (single allocator)
    participant Forms as ast_builder::build_forms (:Type seam)
    participant Form as ast_builder::build_form (per-form dispatch)
    participant Expr as ast_builder::build_expr
    participant Helpers as type/annotation/param/pattern helpers

    Caller->>API: parse / expand / build request
    API->>Reader: source -> Vec<Sexp>
    Note over Reader: Lexes booleans + reader macros (quote/quasiquote/unquote/anon-fn). Dotted-module-path parsing duplicated across read_symbol_or_keyword & read_qualified_tail (F5).

    opt module forms present
        API->>Mod: extract mod/import/export/platform
        Note over Mod: super rewritten eagerly here (BC inv #3, documented). No literal super survives the boundary.
    end

    opt quasiquote present
        API->>QQ: expand_quasiquotes
        QQ->>Span: next_synthetic_span (shared)
        QQ->>QQ: make_sexp_* / make_slist / make_sconcat (DSL #1)
    end

    opt defmacro present
        API->>DM: parse defmacro / synthesize clauses
        DM->>Span: next_synthetic_span (shared, via re-export)
        DM->>DM: make_*_match / make_var_pattern (DSL #2)
        Note over QQ,DM: Two parallel synthetic-Sexp DSLs (F2). Both must match ast_builder reading EXACTLY — hidden contract.
    end

    Note over Caller,Forms: Orchestrator (int) peels begin (flatten_begin) + structural decls (extract_module_declarations) + expands macros BEFORE frontend dispatch (documented caller contract).

    Caller->>Forms: build_forms(&[Sexp])  (single entry — no REPL/batch split)
    loop per sexp
        alt leading :Type annotation
            Forms->>Expr: build_one_expr_at (pairs :Type + following form)
        else top-level form head
            Forms->>Form: is_top_level_form_sexp? -> build_form
            Note right of Form: head-set classification expressed twice (routing predicate :328 vs dispatch :210) — latent skew (F7).
            Form->>Helpers: parse_def_visibility / parse_defn / deftype / deftrait / impl / defmacro
        else bare expression
            Forms->>Expr: build_expr
        end
    end
    Form->>Helpers: annotation / type-expr / param / pattern parsing
    Expr->>Helpers: same shared helpers

    Note right of Form: ast_builder.rs (1211 prod LOC) still mixes top-level + expr + trait/impl + types + patterns in one file — not split per baseline rec #1 (F1). No god function (largest ~75 lines).
    Note right of Helpers: Frontend emits cranelisp_types DTOs only (ParsedEntry/TopLevel/Expr/Sexp). Name resolution deferred to int/typecheck — SymbolRef::new(None, ..) only (lens v clean).
